@page "/components/stat-cards"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.StatCards

<DocsHeader Title="Stat cards" Eyebrow="Data">
    <Lead>KPI cards for dashboards: a label, a large value, a trend and a short description.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>
    <code>StilStatCard</code> is a <a href="components/cards">card</a> with a fixed layout, so a row of them lines up.
    It renders in static server rendering. Format the value yourself, in the user's culture.
</p>

<h2 id="kpis">Values and trends</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Kpis)">
    <p>
        <code>Trend</code> is shown in a badge with an arrow for <code>TrendDirection</code>: green for
        <code>Up</code>, red for <code>Down</code> and gray for <code>Neutral</code>. When up is bad (returns,
        errors, costs), set <code>TrendVariant</code>. Screen readers hear the direction in words, for example
        "up 12.4%"; <code>TrendLabel</code> replaces that text, and <code>UpText</code>, <code>DownText</code> and
        <code>NeutralText</code> translate it. <code>Icon</code> is decorative.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="links">Links and extra content</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(LinksAndContent)">
    <p>
        With <code>Href</code> the whole card is a link to the details. Child content goes under the value, for
        example a progress bar or a <a href="components/charts#sparklines">sparkline</a>.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<ApiTable Type="typeof(StilStatCard)" />
